const infichoiceEditorialSeeds = [
  ['Study abroad is a life decision—not an escape plan', 'Global study', 'Students', 'A foreign campus can widen your world, but only when the course, cost and daily life serve the person you are trying to become.', 'Begin beneath the country name. What work, community or capability are you crossing borders to pursue? Compare that purpose with the compulsory curriculum, teaching style, professional recognition and actual graduate routes.\n\nThen test the complete life: distance from family, climate, language, loneliness, healthcare, food, housing, part-time-work limits and financial exposure. Admission is one milestone inside a larger transition—not proof that the decision fits.', 'Study abroad process 2026', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/study-abroad-process-2026'],
  ['Master’s degree or postgraduate diploma?', 'Course choice', 'Graduates', 'The shorter or cheaper credential is not automatically the practical choice, and the longer degree is not automatically more valuable.', 'Compare the learning outcome first: depth, supervised research, professional accreditation, workplace practice and the roles graduates actually enter. Check whether the credential is recognised for the next degree, regulated profession or jurisdiction you may need.\n\nBuild a full-cost comparison including tuition, living expenses, equipment, travel and foregone earnings. Immigration and work rules change; verify them through current government sources rather than allowing them to become the hidden purpose of the course.', 'Masters vs PG Diploma Abroad: Which Is Better?', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/masters-vs-pg-diploma-abroad-which-is-better-2026-complete-guide'],
  ['Choose a mentor without surrendering your judgment', 'Mentorship', 'Students', 'A good mentor improves the questions, exposes blind spots and helps you verify a plan; they do not manufacture certainty.', 'Ask what experience the mentor has, which countries or disciplines they genuinely understand, how they handle conflicts of interest and what they will not advise on. A testimonial is not a substitute for relevant expertise.\n\nLeave each session with assumptions, sources and actions—not dependency. Verify admissions, visa, scholarship and professional-registration claims independently, and keep the final decision with the student.', 'Why Every Study Abroad Student Needs a Mentor', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/why-every-study-abroad-student-needs-a-mentor-2026-guide'],
  ['Your application needs a control room', 'Admissions', 'Students', 'Strong applications still fail when documents, evidence, finances and deadlines live in scattered chats and memory.', 'Create one tracker for programme requirements, official links, deadlines, references, tests, transcripts, funding, submissions and decisions. Record the date each changing rule was verified.\n\nKeep ambitious, realistic and financially safe options. Proofread every field against source documents, disclose AI assistance where required, and never let generated text invent an achievement or replace your own reason for applying.', 'Study Abroad Application Mistakes to Avoid', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/study-abroad-application-mistakes-to-avoid-2026-guide-for-students'],
  ['Housing belongs in the academic decision', 'Student life', 'Families', 'Housing affects sleep, safety, commute, concentration, belonging and the real cost of a course.', 'Compare university residence, purpose-built student housing, shared rentals and private rooms using the same columns: total monthly cost, deposits, utilities, contract length, commute, accessibility, cooking, security and cancellation terms.\n\nNever transfer money because a listing creates urgency. Verify the provider, inspect by trusted means, read the lease, understand local tenant protections and keep a safe first-arrival plan.', 'Student Accommodation Guide: USA, UK, Canada', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/student-accommodation-guide-usa-uk-canada-2026'],
  ['Furnished or shared housing: compare the ordinary week', 'Student life', 'Students', 'The better room is the one that protects learning, finances and safety—not the one that photographs best.', 'Furnished housing can reduce arrival friction but may cost more or restrict choice. Shared housing can lower costs and build community, but agreements about privacy, cleaning, guests, food and bills matter.\n\nCalculate the complete semester cost and commute. Ask what happens during holidays, who repairs failures, how deposits are protected and whether the student can study and sleep reliably in the space.', 'Furnished vs Shared Student Housing: Pros And Cons', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/furnished-vs-shared-student-housing-pros-amp-cons'],
  ['Compare universities at programme level', 'College choice', 'Families', 'A famous university name cannot tell you which department, curriculum, supervisor or learning environment fits.', 'Compare the exact programme: compulsory modules, assessment, class scale, laboratories, project access, internship support, faculty interests, student services and graduate role evidence. Ranking methodology should become a question list, not a verdict.\n\nSpeak with current students and recent graduates. Ask what surprised them, which promises translated into ordinary experience and what they would verify before making the choice again.', 'Harvard University vs Stanford University: Complete Comparison', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/harvard-university-vs-stanford-university-complete-comparison-2026'],
  ['A short course should produce evidence—not decoration', 'Learning', 'Students', 'Profile-building works when a course closes a real gap and produces work that another person can inspect.', 'Name the capability before enrolling. Check the provider, syllabus, assessment, instructor, prerequisites, accessibility, cost and whether the credential has any recognised meaning.\n\nFinish by applying the learning to a project, research question, community problem or portfolio artifact. Ten unrelated badges communicate less than one difficult piece of work you can explain, critique and improve.', 'Short-Term Courses That Increase Admission Chances for Study Abroad', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/short-term-courses-that-increase-admission-chances-for-study-abroad'],
  ['Compare countries through the life you will actually live', 'Global study', 'Families', 'Country comparisons become misleading when they collapse course quality, cost, work rules and personal fit into one winner.', 'Compare jurisdictions using dated evidence: programme strength, recognition, tuition, living cost, healthcare, safety, climate, language, accessibility, distance from family and current student-work or post-study rules.\n\nUse a scenario budget with currency risk and emergency travel. A destination that suits one student’s field, finances and temperament may be wrong for another. Keep the course and calling above migration marketing.', 'USA vs Canada vs UK: Which Is Better for Indian Students?', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/usa-vs-canada-vs-uk-which-is-better-for-indian-students-2026-guide'],
  ['Diploma routes deserve the same due diligence as degrees', 'Pathways', 'Students', 'A practical credential can be an excellent route when its recognition, teaching and progression are real.', 'Verify the awarding institution, regulator or approval status, workshop or placement access, assessment standard and the roles graduates actually perform. Ask whether credits transfer and which further-study routes remain open.\n\nDo not assume shorter means easier employment. Test the daily craft, inspect equipment and supervision, calculate the whole cost and keep evidence of what you can actually do.', 'Top Diploma Courses in India & USA', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/top-diploma-courses-in-india-amp-usa-fees-colleges-amp-career-opportunities'],
  ['Job-ready skills begin with a target task', 'Employment', 'Graduates', '“Learn AI,” “learn data” or “learn marketing” is too vague to guide serious practice.', 'Collect current job descriptions for one role family and separate recurring tasks from tool names. Identify the smallest capability gap that blocks useful work, then choose learning with practice, feedback and assessment.\n\nBuild one outcome for a real user or problem and explain the decisions unaided. Recheck the role map regularly because tools change faster than judgment, communication and domain responsibility.', 'Top Skill Courses to Get Jobs After Graduation', 'https://www.infichoice.com/article/top-skill-courses-to-get-jobs-after-graduation-2026-guide'],
];

